FWIW, that's just Sourceforge numbers. Anyone who buys an Ubuntu CD
(over 8 million sold last time I saw the numbers) is getting a copy of
nethack.  The same is true of many other Linux distributions, and BSD
users likewise would get it from their ports system rather than from
sourceforge.  Who knows how many players there are, but that's
certainly over 30 million extra copies shipped when you add Slackware
+ Red Hat + SUSE numbers to Ubuntu, probably more in the 50 million
range.

I am certainly _not_ claiming those people all play. But there's a
pretty big overlap between Linux/Unix users and nethack players.
Using the Sourceforge numbers is completely ignoring one of the larger
parts of the player base.

On top of that, people who play online at one of the 13+ public
servers aren't going to show up in the sourceforge numbers.  Some of
those are people who also play locally, so it's tough to know how many
additional players that is.

On top of that, many universities had nethack installed in their
computer clusters during the 1990s, so a lot of kids played without
ever downloading it.

On top of that, people using the more modern interfaces (e.g. Falcon's
Eye, Vulture's Claw, whatever) get those from their respective
projects with the core game bundled in.  So they're not going to show
up in the numbers.  Just looking quickly, Falcon's Eye has another
250,000+ copies downloaded for the windows client for the most recent
version alone.

On top of that, nethack's only been on sourceforge since version
3.2.3; the game was around over a decade before it was even possible
to get it from sourceforge.  All that decade of downloads is
completely missing from the Sourceforge numbers.  Games tend to do
best immediately after they come out, too, but the Internet's also
expanded greatly, so it's hard to say whether more copies of nethack
were distributed in the first decade or in the Sourceforge years.

Bottom line: it's impossible to say exactly how many players there
are, but it's easily upwards of 35 million copies shipped and I'd
guess the lower bound on total people who have played is 3 million,
more likely 6 million ish.


